  "query_preview": "..\nTonight through Friday: The ridge rebounds behind the exiting \ncold front. It will continue the warm, dry conditions with \nclear sky through most of the weekend. Highs will be in the 70s \nto low 80s. Minor heat risk threat continues for those who are \nextremely sensitive to heat and not acclimated to the warmer \ntemperatures this early in the season. Overnight lows will be in\nthe upper 40s and 50s. \n\nThe ridge begins to flatten Sunday into Monday as the Gulf of \nAlaska Low moves into BC. It will press a shortwave into the \nregion and bring another period of gusty winds to the western \nportion of the Inland Northwest. Wind gusts are expected to be \nin the 30-40 mph range (80+ percent probability) for Sunday.\nThere is a low confidence chance for light precip along the \nCanadian border as the wave passes. The region is not expected \nto see much change from the warm, dry conditions through \nTuesday. Temperatures continue to remain above the season \nnormal.\n\nEnsembles continue to have poor agreement on the extended for \nWednesday and Thursday. A trough is expected to swing through \nthe region. Ensembles are split on the timing and strength. The\nforecast is trending to the drier outlook. There is around a 20\npercent probability for the wetter, stronger system to pass\nthrough the Inland Northwest. The temperature outlook is\ntrending slightly cooler. /JDC",
